── FACT BEYOND A `without` LIMIT ───── E0204_allocating_callee.lt:11:51  [E0204]

`digits` allocates, through `List.new`, but `digit_count` says `without alloc`:

  11 │ pub fn digit_count(n: i64) -> i64 without alloc { digits(n).len() }
     │                                           ───── the limit
     │                                                   ^^^^^^^^^

Code under `without alloc` makes no list or string. Let the caller make it, and
take it `inout`: writes through its indexes stay in its storage, as `out[i] = x`
does.
